# Java / Spring conventions

- Controllers return `Mono` or `Flux` — keep the stack reactive end-to-end where possible.
- Put business logic in `service/`, persistence in `repository/`, models in `model/`.
- Kafka producers/consumers belong in `service/` or `config/` — follow existing `FanoutConsumer` / `KafkaProducerService` patterns.
- Use constructor injection; avoid field `@Autowired`.
- Name feed strategies consistently: `PUSH`, `PULL`, `HYBRID` (see `FeedController`).

```java
// Prefer explicit strategy handling over magic strings scattered in code
FeedStrategy strategy = FeedStrategy.fromQueryParam(strategyParam);
```
